{"type":"document","title":"TERMINAL-BENCH: BENCHMARKING AGENTS ON HARD, REALISTIC TASKS IN COMMAND LINE INTERFACES","publisher":"arXiv","published_at":"2026-01-17"}
{"type":"claim","page":1,"subject":"Terminal-Bench 2.0","metric":"volume_count","label":"tasks in computer terminal environments","value":89,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"tasks in benchmark","basis":"actual","quote":"We present Terminal-Bench 2.0: a carefully curated hard benchmark composed of 89 tasks in computer terminal environments inspired by problems from real workflows.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":1,"subject":"frontier models and agents","metric":"index_value","label":"score less than","value":65,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"Terminal-Bench 2.0 benchmark score","basis":"actual","quote":"We show that frontier models and agents score less than 65% on the benchmark and conduct an error analysis to identify areas for model and agent improvement.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":2,"subject":"Claude Code","metric":"revenue_from_operations","label":"run-rate revenue","value":1,"unit":"USD billion","period":"2025","scope":"run-rate revenue","basis":"actual","quote":"For example, as of time of writing Anthropic claims that Claude Code drives $1B in run-rate revenue (Anthropic, 2025).","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":2,"subject":"Terminal-Bench 2.0","metric":"volume_count","label":"challenging tasks","value":89,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"dataset tasks","basis":"actual","quote":"We also introduce the Terminal-Bench 2.0 dataset, a set of 89 challenging tasks that have been manually verified by three human reviewers for correctness.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":2,"subject":"smaller models","metric":"index_value","label":"scoring around","value":15,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"Terminal-Bench 2.0 resolution rate","basis":"actual","quote":"smaller models scoring around 15%.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":2,"subject":"Terminal-Bench","metric":"volume_count","label":"preexisting benchmarks adapted","value":26,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"adapted preexisting benchmarks","basis":"actual","quote":"The flexibility of this specification has allowed us to adapt 26 other preexisting benchmarks into the same format for compatibility with Terminal-Bench (Appendix D).","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":3,"subject":"Terminal-Bench","metric":"headcount","label":"contributors","value":93,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"crowd-sourced task creation","basis":"actual","quote":"In order to design a diverse benchmark, we crowd-sourced tasks through open-source contributions, with 93 contributors creating 229 tasks.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":3,"subject":"Terminal-Bench","metric":"volume_count","label":"creating tasks","value":229,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"contributed tasks","basis":"actual","quote":"In order to design a diverse benchmark, we crowd-sourced tasks through open-source contributions, with 93 contributors creating 229 tasks.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":3,"subject":"Terminal-Bench 2.0","metric":"volume_count","label":"selected tasks for dataset","value":89,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"selected tasks","basis":"actual","quote":"Of those 229, we selected 89 for the Terminal-Bench 2.0 dataset based on the author’s difficulty assessment and a quality assessment by three experienced human reviewers","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":5,"subject":"fix-ocaml-gc task","metric":"volume_count","label":"expert completion time","value":24,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"expert time in hours","basis":"actual","quote":"takes almost 1 day (24 hours) for an expert and ten days (240 hours) for a junior engineer to complete","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":5,"subject":"fix-ocaml-gc task","metric":"volume_count","label":"junior engineer completion time","value":240,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"junior engineer time in hours","basis":"actual","quote":"takes almost 1 day (24 hours) for an expert and ten days (240 hours) for a junior engineer to complete","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":5,"subject":"Software Engineering","metric":"volume_count","label":"Tasks per category","value":26,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"Terminal-Bench 2.0 tasks","basis":"actual","quote":"Software Engineering 26","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":6,"subject":"Terminal-Bench 2.0","metric":"volume_count","label":"state-of-the-art agents evaluated","value":6,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"evaluation setup","basis":"actual","quote":"We evaluate six state-of-the-art agents on Terminal-Bench 2.0 across 16 frontier models.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":6,"subject":"Terminal-Bench 2.0","metric":"volume_count","label":"frontier models evaluated","value":16,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"evaluation setup","basis":"actual","quote":"We evaluate six state-of-the-art agents on Terminal-Bench 2.0 across 16 frontier models.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":6,"subject":"Terminal-Bench 2.0","metric":"volume_count","label":"total trials","value":32155,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"evaluation trials","basis":"actual","quote":"For each supported model and agent combination, we run the benchmark at least five times, resulting in a total of 32,155 trials","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":6,"subject":"GPT-5.2 (Codex CLI)","metric":"index_value","label":"average resolution rate","value":63,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"highest score achieved","basis":"actual","quote":"Codex CLI paired with GPT-5.2 achieves the highest average resolution rate of 63%, followed by Terminus 2 with Claude Opus 4.5 and Terminus 2 with Gemini 3 Pro","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":7,"subject":"Claude Opus 4.5 (Terminus 2)","metric":"index_value","label":"resolution rate","value":58,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"model performance","basis":"actual","quote":"Claude Opus 4.5 and Terminus 2 with Gemini 3 Pro at 58% and 57%, respectively.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":7,"subject":"Gemini 3 Pro (Terminus 2)","metric":"index_value","label":"resolution rate","value":57,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"model performance","basis":"actual","quote":"and Terminus 2 with Gemini 3 Pro at 58% and 57%, respectively.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":7,"subject":"Kimi K2 Thinking (Terminus 2)","metric":"index_value","label":"resolving tasks on average","value":36,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"open-weight models performance","basis":"actual","quote":"with Terminus 2 and Kimi K2 Thinking performing best among the open-weight models, resolving 36% of tasks on average.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":7,"subject":"Codex CLI","metric":"index_value","label":"resolution rate increases","value":52,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"GPT-5.2 vs GPT-5-Nano","basis":"actual","quote":"Codex CLI resolution rate increases by 52% when using GPT-5.2 instead of GPT-5-Nano","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":7,"subject":"Gemini 2.5 Pro","metric":"index_value","label":"increase in resolution rate","value":17,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"Terminus 2 vs OpenHands","basis":"actual","quote":"while Gemini-2.5-Pro sees a 17% increase in resolution rate when paired with Terminus 2 instead of OpenHands","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":8,"subject":"Human-hard tasks","metric":"index_value","label":"empirically hard for models","value":93.3,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"tasks rated hard by humans","basis":"actual","quote":"and 93.3% of human-hard tasks are also empirically hard (Figure 7).","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":8,"subject":"Human-medium tasks","metric":"index_value","label":"models find them hard","value":54.5,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"discrepancy between human medium and empirical hard","basis":"actual","quote":"The largest discrepancy occurs when humans rate tasks as medium but models find them hard (54.5%)","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":8,"subject":"Human-medium tasks","metric":"index_value","label":"empirically medium","value":29.1,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"tasks rated medium by humans","basis":"actual","quote":"A notable share of medium tasks are empirically medium (29.1%) or empirically easy (16.4%)","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":8,"subject":"Human-medium tasks","metric":"index_value","label":"empirically easy","value":16.4,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"tasks rated medium by humans","basis":"actual","quote":"A notable share of medium tasks are empirically medium (29.1%) or empirically easy (16.4%)","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":9,"subject":"annotators","metric":"index_value","label":"calibration agreement","value":93,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"Cohen's kappa on 20 trials","basis":"actual","quote":"On a calibration subset of 20 trials, annotators achieve high agreement (93% Cohen’s-κ).","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":9,"subject":"GPT-5 judge","metric":"index_value","label":"agreement with human annotations","value":90,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"120 human-labeled traces","basis":"actual","quote":"Compared against 120 human-labeled traces, this process achieves the closest alignment with human annotations, with an agreement of 90% (92% precision, 90% recall).","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":9,"subject":"GPT-5 judge","metric":"index_value","label":"precision","value":92,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"alignment with human annotations","basis":"actual","quote":"with an agreement of 90% (92% precision, 90% recall).","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":9,"subject":"GPT-5 judge","metric":"index_value","label":"recall","value":90,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"alignment with human annotations","basis":"actual","quote":"with an agreement of 90% (92% precision, 90% recall).","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":9,"subject":"Grok 4","metric":"index_value","label":"command error rate","value":9.2,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"Terminus 2 trajectories","basis":"actual","quote":"We find that command error rates range from 9.2% (Grok 4) to 26.7% (GPT-OSS-120B).","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":9,"subject":"GPT-OSS-120B","metric":"index_value","label":"command error rate","value":26.7,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"Terminus 2 trajectories","basis":"actual","quote":"We find that command error rates range from 9.2% (Grok 4) to 26.7% (GPT-OSS-120B).","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":10,"subject":"command failures","metric":"volume_count","label":"uniformly sampled and categorized","value":3800,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"failures sampled across tasks and models","basis":"actual","quote":"3,800 failures are uniformly sampled and categorized across Terminal-Bench tasks and models; the results are shown in Figure 9.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":10,"subject":"command failures","metric":"index_value","label":"calling executables that are not installed or not in PATH","value":24.1,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"share of all command failures","basis":"actual","quote":"We find that command failures calling executables that are not installed or not in PATH are the most frequent (24.1% of all failures) followed by failures when running executables (9.6%).","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":10,"subject":"command failures","metric":"index_value","label":"failures when running executables","value":9.6,"unit":"percent","period":null,"scope":"share of all command failures","basis":"actual","quote":"followed by failures when running executables (9.6%).","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":21,"subject":"Terminal-Bench","metric":"volume_count","label":"total recorded trials","value":32155,"unit":"count","period":null,"scope":"agent execution time and token usage","basis":"actual","quote":"Agent execution time and token usage were recorded across all 32,155 trials, and the number of model (API) calls was recorded for Terminus 2 runs.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":28,"subject":"Terminal-Bench","metric":"index_value","label":"Outcome Validity score","value":0.857,"unit":null,"period":null,"scope":"Agentic Benchmark Checklist","basis":"actual","quote":"Overall, Terminal-Bench scores 0.857 on Outcome Validity, 1.000 on Task Validity, and 0.830 on Benchmark Reporting, averaging to 0.896.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":28,"subject":"Terminal-Bench","metric":"index_value","label":"Task Validity score","value":1.000,"unit":null,"period":null,"scope":"Agentic Benchmark Checklist","basis":"actual","quote":"Overall, Terminal-Bench scores 0.857 on Outcome Validity, 1.000 on Task Validity, and 0.830 on Benchmark Reporting, averaging to 0.896.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":28,"subject":"Terminal-Bench","metric":"index_value","label":"Benchmark Reporting score","value":0.830,"unit":null,"period":null,"scope":"Agentic Benchmark Checklist","basis":"actual","quote":"Overall, Terminal-Bench scores 0.857 on Outcome Validity, 1.000 on Task Validity, and 0.830 on Benchmark Reporting, averaging to 0.896.","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":28,"subject":"Terminal-Bench","metric":"index_value","label":"ABC average score","value":0.896,"unit":null,"period":null,"scope":"Agentic Benchmark Checklist","basis":"actual","quote":"averaging to 0.896. This places it near the top of the ABC leaderboard, ranking second among existing benchmarks","keys":{}}
{"type":"claim","page":28,"subject":"Terminal-Bench","metric":"global_rank","label":"ABC leaderboard rank","value":2,"unit":null,"period":null,"scope":"Agentic Benchmark Checklist leaderboard","basis":"actual","quote":"This places it near the top of the ABC leaderboard, ranking second among existing benchmarks, and reflects the substantial care and rigor invested by its developers.","keys":{}}
